==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Havsnejonöga.jpg|thumb|A '''lamprey''']]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|laumprei}}, borrowed from {{bor|en|fro|lampreie}} (modern {{m+|fr|lamproie}}), from {{der|en|ML.|lampreda}}, possibly alteration of {{der|en|LL.|lampetra|t=lamprey}}, whose further origin is unknown, though is [[folk etymology|traditionally]] thought to be a combination of {{m|la|lambō|t=I lick, lap}} + {{m|la|petra|t=stone, rock}}. {{doublet|en|limpet}}, which came straightway from {{m+|la|-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlæm.pɹi/|/ˈlæm.pɹeɪ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-ca-lamprey.opus|Audio (CA)}}
* {{hyphenation|en|lam|prey}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# Any long slender [[primitive]] eel-like [[freshwater]] and saltwater [[fish]] of the [[Petromyzontidae]] [[family]], having a [[sucking]] [[mouth]] with [[rasping]] [[teeth]] but no [[jaw]].

